---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
const description = 'DevOps consulting with Wei-Yu Chen: AWS and Kubernetes architecture, CI/CD, deployment troubleshooting, and operational reliability.';
const schema = { '@type': 'Service', name: 'DevOps and Cloud Consulting', serviceType: 'AWS, Kubernetes and DevOps consulting', description, url: `${site.url}/services/devops/`, provider: { '@id': `${site.url}/#person` } };
---
<Base title="DevOps, AWS & Kubernetes Consulting" description={description} schema={schema}>
  <section class="wrap page-hero"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Services</span></div><div class="eyebrow">02 / DevOps & cloud</div><h1>Infrastructure your team<br />can understand and run.</h1><p class="page-lead">Practical DevOps consulting for AWS and Kubernetes environments. Investigate failures, improve delivery, and make the next infrastructure decision with clearer evidence.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/contact/?topic=devops">Discuss your infrastructure <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><nav class="service-switch" aria-label="Consulting services"><a href="/services/ai-engineering/">AI engineering ↗</a><a href="/services/devops/" aria-current="page">DevOps & cloud</a></nav></section>
  <section class="wrap content-grid"><aside><div class="content-label">MAKE THE SYSTEM LEGIBLE</div><p class="aside-note">The goal is a system your team can reason about, deploy, and recover.</p></aside><div class="prose"><h2>Start with the failure people experience.</h2><p>A deployment that stalls, a service that intermittently fails, or an environment that only one person understands: these are concrete places to start. I help connect the visible symptom to the infrastructure and delivery decisions behind it.</p><p>I work from the current system and available evidence, with a preference for targeted changes and a clear explanation of the tradeoffs.</p><h2>What we can work on</h2><div class="deliverable"><span>01</span><div><h3>AWS & Kubernetes troubleshooting</h3><p>Investigate deployment, networking, access, workload, and infrastructure problems. Establish what changed, narrow the likely cause, and verify the representative user flow after a fix.</p></div></div><div class="deliverable"><span>02</span><div><h3>Delivery pipelines & deployment</h3><p>Review build and release workflows, environment differences, and rollback paths. Simplify the route from a reviewed change to a verifiable deployment.</p></div></div><div class="deliverable"><span>03</span><div><h3>Architecture & operational review</h3><p>Review the infrastructure against actual workload needs. Identify unnecessary moving parts, gaps in visibility, and practical improvements to reliability and maintainability.</p></div></div><h2>Make the change reviewable.</h2><p>We first agree on scope and access. Read-only inspection helps establish the current state. Changes should come with an explanation, a recovery path appropriate to their risk, and a check of the behavior that mattered in the first place.</p><p>A handover can include the findings, implementation changes, operational notes, and remaining limits. The precise deliverables depend on the project.</p><blockquote><p>The best fix makes the system easier to explain the next time something breaks.</p></blockquote><h2>Questions you might be asking</h2><div class="faq"><h3>Does this require rebuilding our infrastructure?</h3><p>Usually that should be a conclusion, rather than the starting assumption. We can investigate the existing setup and identify the smallest useful change first.</p></div><div class="faq"><h3>Can this include an AI application?</h3><p>Yes. The same engagement can cover application integration and the infrastructure it needs to run, with the scope agreed in advance.</p></div><div class="faq"><h3>Is this a managed, on-call service?</h3><p>The services described here are project-based consulting. Ongoing support, response times, and operational ownership would need a separate agreement.</p></div><div class="related"><a href="/writing/eks-irsa-mechanism/">Read: How IAM Roles for Service Accounts Work in EKS <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
  <section class="wrap contact-band"><div><div class="eyebrow">A clearer path forward</div><h2>What is getting in the way?</h2><p>Start with the symptom, the environment, and what you have tried.</p></div><a class="button" href="/contact/?topic=devops">Let’s talk <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>
</Base>
